<p>Lee Atchison is a software architect and author who helps companies
architect and operate AI-powered SaaS at scale.</p>

<p>He focuses on four things: building AI into SaaS products, controlling what
AI costs to run, keeping AI features reliable in production, and designing for
scalability and high availability.</p>

<p>Lee spent seven years at Amazon and AWS, where he helped rearchitect Amazon's
retail website and built AWS Elastic Beanstalk. He then spent eight years at
New Relic, leading the architecture that carried its SaaS observability
platform through rapid growth. He also served as CTO of AI company Product
Genius.</p>

<p>Today he advises companies through his practice, Atchison Technology. He is
the author of <em>Architecting for Scale</em> (O'Reilly, second edition) and
<em>The Software Conductor</em>, and creates courses for O'Reilly, LinkedIn
Learning, and Atchison Academy. He publishes the Software Architecture Insights
newsletter and podcast.</p>

<p>Software Architecture Insights is where Lee shares what he's learning in
real time, from the systems he's working on right now, not from a textbook.
Every Tuesday morning, it's practical thinking on architecture, cloud scale,
and technical leadership from someone still doing the work.</p>

